From 675d77498c32ad61c503c04f39b037ac39831b46 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 22:20:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] The user's token on server-side queries a user started;
 labelled samples in the banner

otel-chdb owner decisions of 2026-09-28 (DECISIONS.md D33):

- Server-side queries a user started carry that user's token. The API runs
  every request's work inside runAsQueryServiceUser (an AsyncLocalStorage
  in common-utils' node client), with the token from the header the OIDC
  proxy sets (HDX_QUERY_SERVICE_TOKEN_HEADER; an MCP or external API client
  sends it beside its access key). Every query the node client sends in
  that work (MCP tools, the external API, the API's own routes: AI
  summaries, Prometheus) goes out with the user's token, so the query
  service scopes and audits it as the user. If the user's token did not
  reach the API, the query fails: it is never sent as the service
  identity. HDX_QUERY_SERVICE_TOKEN_FILE's service identity is left to
  work no user started (the alert task, usage stats).
- Labelled samples: the query service answers HyperDX's flagged read
  samples (allowSampledRead, patch 0001) with completeness "sample" and
  X-Otel-Sample (rows read, the bound, whether reading stopped at it). The
  store records them as samples, never complete, apart from the page's
  label; the banner says on a line of its own that the page's suggestion
  lists are samples and whether they stopped at the bound.
- Fixes patch 0003's completeness.test.ts: the "reads the adapter headers"
  expectation missed atBasis: false (found by running the suite).
